{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1544452-propose-new-birthright-type-stigmata-blessings-curse-mutations-etc","id":1544452,"title":"Propose new Birthright type: Stigmata / Blessings / Curse / Mutations / etc ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-22T04:06:46-07:00","id":1544452,"title":"Propose new Birthright type: Stigmata / Blessings / Curse / Mutations / etc ?","content":"I am in the middle of writting a Pantheon , and my train of thought led me to realize that none of the existing official Birthright categories in Scion 2e account for stuff like Jesus' Stigmata, the curse and mark of Cain or the natural invincibility Achilles and Siegurd received from being dipped into the River Styx and bathing in dragon blood respectively. Stuff tied to a blessing, a curse, a mutation, a mark or some other form of permanent alteration to the character's very body/soul/existence. What would be a good general term for it and how would it work mechanically?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28221-chronorebel","name":"ChronoRebel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T18:16:26-07:00","id":1544612,"title":"","content":"Those, I think, would be in the realm of Edges (described starting on page 115 of <i>Saints &amp; Monsters</i>), specifically the Mythic Edges. Some might also be Pantheon-Specific Knacks or Boons, depending on how powerful you want to make them. You could also raid stuff like Talents from Trinity Continuum for particular blessings and curses.<br /> <br /> If you don't have access to Saints &amp; Monsters, Edges are like Birthrights, except they're character-specific -- they're highly specialized training or unusual talents that don't <i>quite</i> rise to the level of Knacks, and most of them have a flat cost in Birthright dots rather than a 1-5 scale. You could also think of them as similar to Merits from the Chronicles of Darkness games.<br /> <br /> Saints &amp; Monsters also talks about Titanic Scions taking Titanic Mutations in place of Knacks or Boons -- Mutations have a Motif, are tied to a Titanic Calling, and you gain abilities (including one Boon and one Bane) based on how many dots you invest (getting high enough means you also gain a Persistent Condition like a Denizen that had benefits and drawbacks). You don't necessarily need to tie them to Titans if your Pantheon contains sufficiently inhuman members that are part of the structure (like the Shen, Annuna, or Atua, or some interpretations of the Abrahamic faiths I've seen).<br /> <br /> So there are a number of ways you could go about it mechanically, and I recommend <i>Saints &amp; Monsters</i> for just this sort of rules expansion, because I feel that will really work with what you're trying to accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}